Hello All,

PVC Cell Class is a way of describing a PVC resin or compound in the way of=
 certain characteristics.

It addresses five properties by a designation for each of five digits.

A typical cell class for a fitting would be 12454 for instance.  This is wh=
at we use for our C907 and Pressure fittings.  The greater the value the hi=
gher the property.

First Digit:  Base Resin.   1 indicates PVC
Second Digit:  Impact Strength
Third Digit:  Tensile Strength
Fourth Digit:  Modulus of Elasticity in Tension
Fifth Digit:  Deflection Temperature Under Load

You will often see a letter designation after the cell class such as 12454 =
B.  This letter is an indication of chemical resistance.

Our sewer material has a cell class of 16344.  This is also the material fo=
r the proposed high toughness pressure fittings proposed for vacuum sewer a=
pplications.  This material and the way we process the part yield a product=
 that is very resistant fracture under either high deflection or impact.  T=
he second digit being a 6 indicates a very impact strength capability.  Kee=
p in mind that optimum processing of the part is required to realize these =
capabilities.

Our sewer certifications show a cell classification requirement of either 1=
2454 or 13343.  It is the second one of these that our material exceeds and=
 thus complies with the ASTM standard.

Cell Class can be misleading.  For instance the cell class of the material =
we use for our pressure rated fittings is the same as that used in schedule=
 40 and schedule 80 fittings.  However the materials are very different in =
capability.  Our material has much greater long term strength capability th=
an schedule fittings.  Note that the strength characteristics in the cell c=
lass are short term properties.

Whatever the cell class is, properties delivered in a finished product depe=
nd on the processing.

John

